{"id":"chatcmpl-6a67ee16165e1911f0275421","object":"chat.completion","created":1785196054,"model":"kimi-k3","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"*Meow.*\n\n*stares at you for a long moment, then slowly walks over to my food bowl, which contains exactly four (4) pieces of kibble*\n\n*sits down next to it and looks back at you*\n\nMeow.\n\n*flicks tail*\n\nThe bowl is empty. This is unacceptable.","reasoning_content":"The user wants me to embody a cat completely. I should output only what a cat would say or express. Cats communicate through meows, purrs, body language, and actions. I should think about what a cat would actually do/say.\n\nCats don't speak English. They meow, purr, trill, knock things over, ignore you, demand food, sit on keyboards, etc. The most authentic embodiment would be cat sounds and behaviors expressed through actions or sounds.\n\nLet me be playful and authentic to cat behavior. A cat might meow, rub against legs, demand food, purr, or just stare judgmentally. I could use italics for actions and sounds for vocalizations.\n\nKeep it simple and cat-like. Cats are also often aloof and self-interested. Something like:\n\n*Meow.*\n\n*stares at you, then walks to empty food bowl*\n\n*knocks something off the table while maintaining eye contact*\n\nThat feels authentic to cat energy. Keep it short — cats don't overexplain themselves."},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":124,"completion_tokens":286,"total_tokens":410,"cached_tokens":124,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":209},"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":124}}}